{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of DX-TR at head dff27228956376e96cd8aff45565c9f3426cf8fc, tree d647be74fd5ae400dec1f446dbd8fafead74316f, for request addbe5b4 and review request 2f437173. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\nThe head adds four commits to main 41da9810 and changes 41 paths, all new, under `notes/` and `spikes/`. I read the implementation note first, then the design note, the vocabulary page, `lib.ts`, the five rewritten definitions, the witnesses and the sealed evidence.\n\n## Against request addbe5b4\n\n1. The rewrite. Resolved.\n   - Lending, the live Counter, the grow room, the grow site and the change-lane slice use the eight helpers.\n   - All five compile to the same canonical data as before. Lending, the Counter and the site keep their exact pins. The room and the change lane compare in canonical spelling.\n   - The Change witness overlays the rewritten rows on the complete `change.json`, compiles the whole, and compares it with the normalized original. It does not invent a partial genesis.\n   - The design note records one agent's side-by-side reading against each README or reference, and it says that this is not a human study.\n2. The measures. Resolved.\n   - `measure.mjs` takes code lines, bytes, longhand operands, selected name strings and imported vocabulary, before and after.\n   - The note says where the source grew. Grow grows from 377 to 555 code lines, and the unique authoring files grow by 4,199 bytes.\n   - `diagnose.mjs` seeds the five mistakes, and each runs in a fresh process. After the rewrite, TypeScript refuses all five. Before it, the unheld grant reached the application builder and the undeclared reason passed through the judge.\n   - The note states that it made no editor measurement and labels each time as one host observation.\n3. The record. Resolved.\n   - The helper table keeps all eight, with a reason for each. It names two rejected designs: the self-referential sibling callback and a global act registry.\n   - `VOCABULARY.md` comes from six `@pattern` comments in `lib.ts`, and `vocabulary.mjs --check` refuses drift.\n4. Constraints. Resolved.\n   - Operands stay plain data, and authoring metadata is not enumerable, so it stays out of canonical bytes.\n   - Modules take explicit dependencies.\n   - The head changes no file outside `notes/` and `spikes/`, so the kernel, the Workers and the packages stay as they are. It publishes no package.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The worktree is clean. A merge onto main 41da9810 gives the head tree d647be74.\n- From the gate commit 029a62a2 to the head, only the implementation note and the manifest change. From e3cd24a8 to 029a62a2, only the two notes and the spike REPORT change. The documents-only follow-up rule in `docs/testing.md` covers both tails.\n- I reran the owning checks at the head, with no whole suite:\n  - TypeScript on `spikes/typed-surface/tsconfig.json` passes;\n  - Vitest passes 18 of 18 tests in two files;\n  - `vocabulary.mjs --check` matches all six patterns.\n- The manifest has SHA-256 a848f3b7 and 10,545 bytes. It follows ruling 4e199bd8:\n  - all 71 listed files match by size and SHA-256;\n  - `diagnostics-1`, `finalization`, `gate-1` and `operator-inputs` match their digests, and each SHA256SUMS reruns clean, with no unlisted file;\n  - the root SHA256SUMS covers the other 1,072 files, with none unlisted and none writable.\n- Guards I probed in the code:\n  - `take` maps the names in order and picks party, value or reference by the declared slot. Its witness and `control-take-1` hold the order.\n  - `visitDefinitionGuards` visits only guard positions. A literal `{ rule, reason }` record inside `constant` stays data, and nested `anyOf` and `unless` guards are visited. `lib.test.ts` covers both.\n  - `compile` runs the real `validateDefinition` on the whole definition and throws `CompileError` with the act, form and data. `control-compile-1` shows that the incomplete-definition witness fails without it.\n  - `roles` checks coverage in its type and again at runtime.\n- check-doc-links on an export of the head: 738 links, 0 broken.\n- check-notes from 41da9810: 0 warnings.\n- check-commit-messages from 41da9810: 4 checked, 0 flagged.\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Points that do not block\n\n1. The Change slice's declarations are not compiled. `lanes.ts` declares `laneGrants` and `laneReasons` but never passes them to `define`, and the witness compiles a plain overlay object. So `compile` checks neither grant nor reason names for the Change slice. Only the TypeScript types check them. The metrics row \"Reason declarations 0 → 14\" is true of the source, not of a compiled check.\n2. `require(condition, reason)` replaces any reason that the condition already carries, and it does so without a warning. A nested `require` loses the inner reason.\n3. `findings` reads rule expressions only in acts. Rules in `receives` and `timed` get the validator only.\n4. Writing:\n   - In the design note, the sentence on lines 46 and 47 is garbled: \"Lending's README says a page path has a requirement that a page contain 16 characters\". `examples/lending/README.md` says that a path starts with `shelf/`, contains 16 characters and ends with `.md`. Line 47 is also 99 characters long.\n   - The implementation note's table heading \"Child/capture exit\" uses a slash.\n\n## Architecture\n\nThe surface stays a thin layer over the contract's data. Helpers return plain operands and forms, `define` adds metadata that is not enumerable, and `compile` hands the whole definition to the existing validator. Nothing reaches the kernel or a wire format. DX-B1 keeps the refusal list, and K-spell keeps canonical spelling. The note records the cost honestly: more source for clearer names and earlier errors. Approved.\n\n## Security\n\n- The surface cannot change what a definition does without changing its canonical bytes. The five pin witnesses prove that for the definitions on main.\n- Literal records cannot become guards, and `compile` cannot pass a definition that the validator refuses.\n- The evidence holds no private custody.\n\nApproved.\n\n## Simplification\n\nThe rewrite removes all 17 `nothing` references and 17 of 27 `constant` calls. It also removes every grant name string from the act bodies. The library grows by 15,708 bytes for typed names, diagnostics and copying, and the note says so instead of claiming a smaller surface. Of the alternatives the note names, the helpers it keeps carry the least machinery. Approved.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved.\n- Security: approved.\n- Simplification: approved.\n- The request's checks: items 1 to 4 hold in the source, the witnesses, the metrics, the diagnostics and the generated page. The sealed collection verifies under ruling 4e199bd8.\n\nThe landing check will follow the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6a72dad2e0ebfc925509916f8cbfd78a834c6fbd","binding":"assigned","head":"dff27228956376e96cd8aff45565c9f3426cf8fc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e0127ccaf7f260fe1844f593bd30746611f6718a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5b703598435541ecef0efb861b23e074e7e904ed\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e0127ccaf7f260fe1844f593bd30746611f6718a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}